<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Västergötland</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as West Gothland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Västergötland is a historical province in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, between lakes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-vanern">Vänern</a> and Vättern and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kattegat">Kattegat</a> coast. The core land of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geats">Geats</a>, it had an early bishopric at Skara and its own law, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vastgotalagen">Västgötalagen</a>. It was joined to the Swedish kingdom around 1000, and much of its coast was long contested with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vastergotland.jpg" alt="Västergötland" width="320" height="729" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lapplänning (highlighting by Lokal_Profil) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sverigekarta-Landskap_V%C3%A4sterg%C3%B6tland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
